{"parentUuid":"0fd4cfe7-3872-40ea-b2be-25c8f6c1bcfc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"a74ae8cc6fe515f14","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cfqdq7od5gHZt1VhWFHhHP","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  When a tool that ran fails (a command exiting non-zero, a file tool's\n  error), a failure hook fires instead of the success\n  hook, carrying an error message, whether it was an interrupt, and how long\n  the call took.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#posttoolusefailure\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#posttoolusefailure-input\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bashfail\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-errors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-invalid-input\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no MCP tools and never aborts a running tool, so an\n          MCP tool's error result and an interrupt (is_interrupt true) are not\n          modeled, nor are the truncation marker and timeout lines Claude Code\n          adds to a long or timed-out command's error. Only a missing file's\n          Read error is worded as Claude Code words it; other file tools'\n          errors are the mock's own text.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          A Bash whose shell cannot start (a bare failure message with no\n          \"Exit code N\" line) is not modeled: the mock's Bash always runs\n          /bin/sh, and Claude Code falls back to another shell when\n          CLAUDE_CODE_SHELL names one that does not work, so neither side\n          can produce it. Of input validation, only a missing required\n          parameter is modeled; a parameter of the wrong type or an unknown\n          tool name is not.\n  codex:\n    supported: false\n    reason: Codex's hook events list has no tool-failure event; PostToolUse is its only after-tool event.\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#hooks\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#posttoolusefailure\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#posttooluse\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-failure\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/file-tools\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock runs the Shell, Read and Write tools only, and never aborts\n          a running tool, so the failures of the other tools (MCP tools, Delete,\n          Grep, Task), a timeout (failure_type \"timeout\") and an interrupt\n          (is_interrupt true) are not modeled.\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"sessionStart\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"sessionEnd\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"preToolUse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUseFailure\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"subagentStart\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"subagentStop\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\nversion: 2026.09.28\ncommand: cursor-agent -p --force --trust --model auto --output-format stream-json","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b1d94c5c-0434-4428-8ac7-daf0f03f0818","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:47:01.057Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0fd4cfe7-3872-40ea-b2be-25c8f6c1bcfc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a74ae8cc6fe515f14","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"cla